          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vpkM8",
              "name": "V title",
              "fill": "$ink",
              "content": "UX comparison — which to ship for pilot?",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 18,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "uwzbC",
              "name": "V c",
              "fill": "$muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "C wins consistency: one navigation model, faster to build, desktop stays familiar. Field path is Home → Work → detail → Continue report (3–4 taps). Scan and time logging are secondary (More or WO detail).",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "P6tew",
              "name": "V d",
              "fill": "$muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "D wins field speed: Start next is the first screen, Complete work is a large primary, Scan and Time are first-class tabs. Cost: two shells (tech phone vs admin desktop), more QA, and role detection before chrome renders.",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "TYWZ6",
              "name": "V rec",
              "fill": "$teal",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Recommendation: ship C for the PWA pilot (already coded). Prototype D’s Queue + Start next pattern inside C’s Work tab as a follow-up experiment — borrow D’s action hierarchy without forking the whole shell.",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "600"
